Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: close PON channels through descriptor reclamation

Retain each mapped descriptor's T-CONT channel and expose an IRQ-safe,
nonblocking channel quiesce operation. Prevent reopening for the attachment
lifetime and distinguish pending DMA mappings from a completed native drain.
FE and optical FIFO retirement remain separate requirements.

Keep IRQ state consistent through PON admission and native queue locks;
ordinary Ethernet still uses its netdev TX lock.

